//! walk rows (walk 1 and walk 3, segments 2 and 18, our capfront rows 1..63) with a free lane at EVERY record.  Switch ON = false.
//!
//! What it changes (both forward regions alike; offsets = record offsets inside the region's FWD_LEN = 58,918,653 generated rows,
//! identical for the two regions, MEASURED):
//!  (1) NOOP: 4,516 records "CX H1 -> x" whose control H1 is ZERO on every valid input are identities; each is replaced in place by
//!      a BitStore0 of the classical bit SCR (65499, unused in the forward rows and 0 there: hybrid.rs uses it only in the reverse
//!      rows, which end by clearing it), a record that names no lane.  Why H1 is 0 there (DERIVED + MEASURED): H1 (his id 642,
//!      generator wire F2 = 387) is ONE at P_2 on every valid input (hs1's canonical state H0..H4 = 0, 1, 0, 0, j* mod 2; the
//!      capped rows use F1..F4 only as dirty loans and restore them); in each increment gadget that lends H1 in its dirty word
//!      the word is complemented, so H1 is 0 when its CX's run.  MEASURED: algebraic replay of the region from the structural entry
//!      (H1 = 1, H0 = H2 = H3 = 0, Z0 = 1, bank[25..128) = 0, EVERY other lane an independent symbol, 4 random points of
//!      GF(2^64)): H1 is the zero polynomial before each of the 4,516 records (fl/tools walg / wnoop).  2,234 of them were the
//!      planner's one-record no-free runs (the record named the only free lane H1).
//!  (2) Z0LOAN: one multi-control ladder (capfront loan call #14,286, row 63) lends Z0 (his id 512 = big[256], ZERO there: U < 2^63)
//!      as a dirty ancilla; its 8 records naming Z0 name instead the passenger lane of his id Y239 (id 495, generator wire 629),
//!      a data lane that no generated row names (MEASURED: never named in either region, nonzero on every pool shot).  A dirty
//!      ancilla's value never matters (the ladder restores it), so the swap is exact for every input; Z0 then stays 0 and
//!      unnamed through the ladder (the planner pool's two 136-record runs).
